WEBVTT

NOTE MPI in your browser: captions match the on-screen steps.

1
00:00:00.201 --> 00:00:04.451
Step 1 of 14. Open the MPI lab: one Web Worker per MPI rank, running the ported algorithm.

2
00:00:04.451 --> 00:00:10.929
Step 2 of 14. Generate the seeded synthetic file: seed 2023, 100,000 tweets in bigTwitter.json's layout.

3
00:00:10.929 --> 00:00:19.465
Step 3 of 14. Run on 1 rank first: the clean baseline, like the 1 node × 1 core job.

4
00:00:19.465 --> 00:00:28.178
Step 4 of 14. Run on 8 ranks: each scans its own byte range, then ranks 0, 1 and 2 reduce the tasks.

5
00:00:28.178 --> 00:00:35.092
Step 5 of 14. Same three result files as the 1-rank baseline; the answers from the task ranks.

6
00:00:35.092 --> 00:00:54.282
Step 6 of 14. Benchmark: 5 timed rounds per worker count after a warm-up, in shuffled order.

7
00:00:54.282 --> 00:01:02.293
Step 7 of 14. Speedup with nominal 95% bootstrap intervals, the fitted Amdahl curve and its band.

8
00:01:02.293 --> 00:01:07.057
Step 8 of 14. Per worker count: median time with an exact interval, efficiency and Karp–Flatt.

9
00:01:07.057 --> 00:01:12.576
Step 9 of 14. Ask the results: optional, answered only from the result tables, with your own key.

10
00:01:12.576 --> 00:01:20.295
Step 10 of 14. AI settings: the key stays in this browser and goes only to the provider.

11
00:01:20.295 --> 00:01:25.538
Step 11 of 14. For this demo: a placeholder key, never a real one; provider calls are intercepted. (Mocked AI response for illustration.)

12
00:01:25.538 --> 00:01:38.293
Step 12 of 14. A mocked answer, labelled AI-generated, with cited rows and an automatic check. (Mocked AI response for illustration.)

13
00:01:38.293 --> 00:01:46.180
Step 13 of 14. Accept it: the review is recorded in the AI audit log, with JSON and CSV export. (Mocked AI response for illustration.)

14
00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:52.049
Step 14 of 14. Forget key: the placeholder is removed from this browser.
